From e5c5a976eef44a9e3977b7300af8a404350bdde5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:17:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08108/11362] The pre-registered primary was circular after
 all: the swap was graded against a stand-in

Adversarial review disputed the one number the O4 -> O6 primary swap rested on. Verified
independently before applying, and the review is right.

Running the SHIPPED `LocalGGUFProposer._goal_defects` -- not a reimplementation of it -- over
the same 115 frozen engines: it keeps 4, and 4 of 4 are O6-positive. FN=0,
P(O6 | accept) = 1.000 against P(O6 | reject) = 0.027. O6 carries the EXACT defect that
disqualified O4.

Root cause, which is the part worth keeping. `pre/circularity_gap.json` computes constancy with
a local `const()` over ALL shown frames and keeps 6, of which 2 fail O6 -- that is the "2 of the
6 the gate would keep still FAIL O6" the swap was justified on. The shipped gate probes at most
`_GOAL_PROBE_MAX_GRIDS = 12` grids, and capping can only make a predicate look MORE constant, so
the shipped gate is strictly stricter: it rejects exactly those two tu93 cells. The two cells
that made O6 look undetermined are the two the cap removes. When a design decision turns on what
a gate would do, call the gate.

This does NOT touch the headline. The regression finding is differential ATTRITION (17/21 vs
1/22 hard induction failures), measured on cells that never reach an outcome, so it is
independent of which outcome was chosen. The primary was already reported as uninterpretable for
that reason; this is a second, independent reason it was never valid.

Also corrected, each verified first:
  * `it_is_pre_existing_not_caused_here` was FALSE. Each of the 7 artifacts already carried an
    acknowledgement pinning HEAD's module sha EXACTLY, so they were fresh at HEAD and the
    refusal was caused by this session's edit. The stated remedy was wrong too: the diff is
    comment-only, so an acknowledgement is the designed, precedented fix. Applied -- lint now
    exits 0, and the appends are provably append-only (0 leaves removed or changed across all 7).
  * A worktree is NOT a sound way to measure this. The first attempt reported two OTHER
    artifacts as pre-existing-stale; they record ABSOLUTE dependency paths that resolve back
    into the main checkout from any worktree. Comparing a pinned sha against `git show HEAD:`
    needs no worktree and is the sound check.
  * The re-ask block is not fully bootstrap-free. Bullets 1-2 are properties of the answer;
    bullet 3 ("prefer a condition on a specific region") is a distributional prior about the
    SHAPE of ARC win conditions, from the taxonomy over the 25 SOLVED public games. Disclosed,
    not removed: it is game-agnostic and would still function on a game nobody has solved.
  * Stale interim counts ("16 of 20 against 1 of 20") corrected to the final 17/21 vs 1/22 in
    both the module comment and the test docstring.
  * detector_coverage presentation: the defect kinds OVERLAP (113 kind-instances over 109
    engines), and `rejection_rate` and `agreement_rate` are different quantities that coincide.
  * tn36 is a weaker existence proof than the anatomy claimed -- this project's own metric
    validity artifact calls its perfect-fidelity engines progress-BAR TICKERS and leaves it out
    in a driver check (AUC 0.6085 -> 0.5316).

Module change is comment-only and PROVEN INERT BY AST IDENTITY: `ast.dump(ast.parse(src))` at
HEAD and in the working tree are identical, 0 added non-comment lines, 0 deletions. The
acknowledgement writer asserts both and refuses to write otherwise.

Flags remain default OFF. No game solved, no level banked, nothing submitted.
adversarial_verify: 0 flags. 80 tests pass; mutation check clean.

